module contract;

// LZ4 stream state reset — resource-projection vocabulary version 1.
//
// Card W37-CORPUS-CONTRACTS-4. ONE TRUSTED ASSUMPTION about one upstream
// function. This module verifies nothing: the C body is not analyzed by this
// loader, and a declaration is a premise.
//
// Read from the pinned checkout at Fluent Bit
// 66910c10a4d7eafa810b84229cf2dcf7b0f26f97 on this card's own run.
//
// ## Why this callee
//
// `LZ4_resetStream` is the SOLE blocker of one projected function,
// `LZ4_resetStreamState` (`lib/librdkafka-2.15.0/src/lz4.c:2706-2711`), whose
// single leaf is the call at `:2709`.
//
// This module is the sibling of `librdkafka/kafka_mem.qcore`, whose
// `rd_kafka_mem_free` declaration card W36-CORPUS-CONTRACTS-3 landed to free
// `LZ4_freeStream`, `LZ4_freeStreamDecode`, `LZ4_freeHC` and
// `LZ4_freeStreamHC` in this same unit. Those are the RELEASE half of the LZ4
// stream lifecycle; this is the RESET half, and it releases nothing.
//
// ## The body, read from `lib/librdkafka-2.15.0/src/lz4.c:1524-1528`
//
//     /* resetStream is now deprecated,
//      * prefer initStream() which is more general */
//     void LZ4_resetStream (LZ4_stream_t* LZ4_stream)
//     {
//         DEBUGLOG(5, "LZ4_resetStream (ctx:%p)", LZ4_stream);
//         MEM_INIT(LZ4_stream, 0, sizeof(LZ4_stream_t_internal));
//     }
//
//   * `LZ4_stream` is WRITTEN THROUGH and nothing else: `MEM_INIT` is
//     `memset`, zeroing `sizeof(LZ4_stream_t_internal)` bytes at the pointer.
//     The object is NOT freed — `LZ4_freeStream` (`:1536`) is the function that
//     does that, and it is a different name — not stored anywhere that outlives
//     the call, and not transferred. The caller's obligation to free the stream
//     it allocated is exactly what it was before the call, which is what
//     `resource_borrowed` says.
//   * `DEBUGLOG` expands to nothing unless `LZ4_DEBUG` is set, which it is not
//     in the pinned build; even when it expands it only formats the POINTER
//     VALUE and writes to `stderr`, taking no custody.
//   * The result is `void`, so `resource_return_none()` is the faithful — and
//     the only faithful — result mode.
//   * The body dereferences (memsets through) its parameter immediately with no
//     guard, so `LZ4_resetStream(NULL)` is upstream undefined behaviour. That is
//     NOT expressible here and is NOT claimed: v1 carries a nullability marker
//     only on a RELEASED parameter, and this one is borrowed. Contrast
//     `LZ4_freeStream` at `:1536`, whose first statement IS
//     `if (!LZ4_stream) return 0;  /* support free on NULL */` — the two
//     neighbours genuinely differ, which is why only one of them could carry a
//     marker even if the vocabulary allowed it on a borrow.
//
// ## Zeroing is not releasing, and that distinction is the whole declaration
//
// A `memset` to zero over a stream context DISCARDS the context's internal
// dictionary pointers. It does not free them, and this projection does not
// model them: `LZ4_stream_t_internal`'s `dictionary` field points into a
// caller-supplied buffer that LZ4 never owns. So the reset creates no leak this
// projection can see and discharges no obligation either. Recorded rather than
// implied.
//
// ## The duty gate (constraint 8)
//
// The body is defined in `lib/librdkafka-2.15.0/src/lz4.c`, which IS one of the
// 185 analysed units (87 projected functions in the baseline), so the duty gate
// applies. This declaration is the NEUTRAL ELEMENT — the one formal `Borrowed`,
// result `None` — the weakest statement the vocabulary can make (constraint 4's
// `N(m)`), so a derived summary can contradict it only by claiming the formal
// is released, transferred, delivered or restored. The body does none of those.
// Any conflict would be a `SummaryConflict` with the declaration governing,
// never a silent override — the shape card W36-CORPUS-CONTRACTS-3 measured for
// `rd_kafka_mem_free` in this same library.
//
// ## ABI (constraint 8)
//
//     lib/librdkafka-2.15.0/src/lz4.h:834
//         LZ4LIB_API void LZ4_resetStream (LZ4_stream_t* streamPtr);
//
// One definition in the whole tree, external linkage. `LZ4LIB_API` is a
// visibility/linkage decoration that changes no type, arity or calling
// convention. `LZ4_stream_t *` is one object-pointer level, `ptr<mut, u8>`; the
// `void` result is `unit`. The header spells the parameter `streamPtr` where
// the definition spells it `LZ4_stream`; a declaration's parameter NAMES are
// its own — the ABI comparison is over types, pointer levels and arity — and
// this module follows the DEFINITION's spelling, the disagreement being
// recorded here rather than silently resolved.
//
// ## NOT CLAIMED
//
//   * Nothing about LZ4 compression correctness, the stream's usability after
//     the reset, or the deprecation the comment announces.
//   * Nothing about `sizeof(LZ4_stream_t_internal)` matching the allocated
//     object's size. A `memset` of the wrong length is an upstream
//     out-of-bounds write this declaration neither creates nor detects.
//   * Nothing about thread safety.
//
// ## Read at the same time and DELIBERATELY LEFT UNDECLARED
//
// `LZ4_resetStream_fast` (`:1532`), `LZ4_initStream`, `LZ4_prepareTable` and
// `LZ4_freeStream` (`:1536`) were all read beside this body and none is
// declared: `LZ4_freeStream` is already decided through
// `librdkafka/kafka_mem.qcore`'s `rd_kafka_mem_free`, and none of the others is
// the sole blocker of any projected function in the baseline.

// --- the deprecated in-place reset of an LZ4 compression stream context ---
extern fn LZ4_resetStream(LZ4_stream: ptr<mut, u8>) -> unit
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(LZ4_stream);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
